    "title": "<p>Common driver mutations and somatic genetic alterations in high-grade follicular cell&ndash;derived non-anaplastic thyroid carcinoma compared with those in well-differentiated and undifferentiated (anaplastic) thyroid carcinomas</p>",
    "legend": "",
    "source": "Giovanni Tallini",
    "copyright": "",
    "tablehtml": "<table class=\"MsoNormalTable\" style=\"width: 797.312px; border-collapse: collapse;\" border=\"0\" width=\"101%\" cellspacing=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\">\r\n<tbody>\r\n<tr style=\"break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 367.844px; border-top: 1pt solid windowtext; border-left: none; border-bottom: 1pt solid windowtext; border-right: none; background: #8db3e2; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" colspan=\"2\" width=\"47%\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif; text-align: center;\" align=\"center\"><strong><span lang=\"EN-GB\">Well-differentiated thyroid carcinoma</span></strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 201.375px; border-right: none; border-bottom: none; border-left: none; border-image: initial; border-top: 1pt solid windowtext; background: #8db3e2; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" rowspan=\"2\" width=\"27%\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><strong><span lang=\"EN-GB\">High-grade follicular cell&ndash;derived non-anaplastic carcinoma</span></strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 184.969px; border-right: none; border-bottom: none; border-left: none; border-image: initial; border-top: 1pt solid windowtext; background: #8db3e2; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" rowspan=\"2\" width=\"25%\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><strong><span lang=\"EN-GB\">Anaplastic thyroid carcinoma</span></strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 168.844px; border: none; background: #8db3e2; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"22%\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><strong><span lang=\"EN-GB\">Follicular carcinoma<sup>a</sup></span></strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 184.625px; border: none; background: #8db3e2; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"24%\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><strong><span lang=\"EN-GB\">Papillary carcinoma</span></strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 168.844px; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"22%\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><em><span lang=\"EN-GB\">RAS</span></em><span lang=\"EN-GB\">: 30&ndash;50%<sup>b</sup></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><em><span lang=\"EN-GB\">TERT</span></em><span lang=\"EN-GB\">: 10&ndash;35%<sup>c</sup></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><em><span lang=\"EN-GB\">PIK3CA</span></em><span lang=\"EN-GB\">: 0&ndash;10%</span></p>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><em><span lang=\"EN-GB\">PTEN</span></em><span lang=\"EN-GB\">: 0&ndash;10%</span></p>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\">Gene fusions (mostly <em>PAX8</em>::<em>PPARG</em>): 10&ndash;50%</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 184.625px; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"24%\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><em><span lang=\"PT\">BRAF</span></em><span lang=\"PT\"> p.V600E: 40&ndash;80%</span></p>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><em><span lang=\"PT\">TERT</span></em><span lang=\"PT\">: 5&ndash;15%<sup>c</sup></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><em><span lang=\"PT\">RAS</span></em><span lang=\"PT\">: 0&ndash;10%<sup>b</sup></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\">Gene fusions (<em>RET</em><sup>d</sup>, <em>NTRK1</em><sup>e</sup>, <em>NTRK3</em><sup>e</sup>, <em>BRAF</em>, others): 5&ndash;25%</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 201.375px; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"27%\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><em><span lang=\"EN-GB\">RAS</span></em><span lang=\"EN-GB\">: 20&ndash;50%<sup>b</sup></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><em><span lang=\"EN-GB\">TERT</span></em><span lang=\"EN-GB\">: 20&ndash;50%<sup>c</sup></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><em><span lang=\"EN-GB\">TP53</span></em><span lang=\"EN-GB\">: 10&ndash;35%</span></p>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><em><span lang=\"PT\">BRAF</span></em><span lang=\"PT\"> p.V600E: 1&ndash;35%<sup>h</sup></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><em><span lang=\"PT\">PTEN</span></em><span lang=\"PT\">: 5&ndash;20%</span></p>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><em><span lang=\"EN-GB\">PIK3CA</span></em><span lang=\"EN-GB\">: 0&ndash;15%</span></p>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><em><span lang=\"EN-GB\">EIF1AX</span></em><span lang=\"EN-GB\">: 5&ndash;15%<sup>f</sup></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\">Gene fusions (<em>RET</em>, <em>ALK</em>, others): 5&ndash;25%</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 184.969px; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"25%\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><em><span lang=\"EN-GB\">TP53</span></em><span lang=\"EN-GB\">: 40&ndash;80%</span></p>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><em><span lang=\"EN-GB\">TERT</span></em><span lang=\"EN-GB\">: 30&ndash;75%<sup>c</sup></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><em><span lang=\"EN-GB\">RAS</span></em><span lang=\"EN-GB\">: 10&ndash;50%<sup>b</sup></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><em><span lang=\"EN-GB\">BRAF</span></em><span lang=\"EN-GB\"> p.V600E: 10&ndash;50%</span></p>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><em><span lang=\"EN-GB\">PIK3CA</span></em><span lang=\"EN-GB\">: 5&ndash;25%</span></p>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><em><span lang=\"EN-GB\">PTEN</span></em><span lang=\"EN-GB\">: 10&ndash;15%</span></p>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><em><span lang=\"EN-GB\">EIF1AX</span></em><span lang=\"EN-GB\">: 5&ndash;15%<sup>f</sup></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\">Gene fusions (<em>RET</em>, others): 0&ndash;5%</span></p>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\">MMR genes: 10&ndash;15%</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 168.844px; background: #daeef3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"22%\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\">Can be genetically unstable and aneuploid, median number of mutations: &le;&nbsp;5<sup>g</sup></span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 184.625px; background: #daeef3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"24%\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\">Genetically stable, median number of mutations: 1&nbsp;&plusmn;&nbsp;1<sup>g</sup></span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 201.375px; background: #daeef3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"27%\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\">Genetically unstable, aneuploid, median number of mutations: 2&nbsp;&plusmn;&nbsp;3<sup>g</sup></span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 184.969px; background: #daeef3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"25%\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\">Genetically unstable, highly aneuploid, median number of mutations: 6&nbsp;&plusmn;&nbsp;5<sup>g</sup></span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 168.844px; border-top: none; border-right: none; border-left: none; border-image: initial; border-bottom: 1pt solid windowtext; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"22%\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><em><span lang=\"PT\">RAS</span></em><span lang=\"PT\">-like TCGA molecular profile<sup>h</sup></span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 184.625px; border-top: none; border-right: none; border-left: none; border-image: initial; border-bottom: 1pt solid windowtext; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"24%\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><em><span lang=\"PT\">BRAF</span></em><span lang=\"PT\"> p.V600E&ndash;like TCGA molecular profile<sup>h</sup></span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 201.375px; border-top: none; border-right: none; border-left: none; border-image: initial; border-bottom: 1pt solid windowtext; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"27%\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\">PDTC: <em>RAS</em>-like TCGA molecular profile<sup>h</sup></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\">HGDTC: <em>BRAF</em> p.V600E&ndash;like TCGA molecular profile<sup>h</sup></span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 184.969px; border-top: none; border-right: none; border-left: none; border-image: initial; border-bottom: 1pt solid windowtext; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"25%\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\">Mostly <em>BRAF</em> p.V600E&ndash;like TCGA molecular profile due to high MAPK transcriptional output regardless of the driver mutation<sup>h</sup></span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n</tbody>\r\n</table>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\">HGDTC, high-grade differentiated thyroid carcinoma; MMR, mismatch repair; PDTC, poorly differentiated thyroid carcinoma; TCGA: The Cancer Genome Atlas.</span></p>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><sup><span lang=\"EN-GB\">a</span></sup><span lang=\"EN-GB\">Encapsulated</span><span lang=\"EN-GB\"> follicular-variant papillary thyroid carcinomas, with invasion or without invasion (non-invasive follicular thyroid neoplasm with papillary-like nuclear features), have molecular alterations similar to those of follicular carcinoma. <sup>b</sup>Mutations in <em>NRAS</em>, <em>HRAS</em>, and <em>KRAS</em>; <em>NRAS</em> is the gene most frequently mutated. <sup>c</sup><em>TERT</em> promoter mutations: p.C228T (c.-124G&gt;A) and p.C250T (c.-146G&gt;A). <sup>d</sup>The prevalence of <em>RET</em>-rearranged cases is higher in children and young patients and in radiation-associated papillary carcinoma. <sup>e</sup>The prevalence of <em>NTRK</em> rearrangements is variably reported as 0&ndash;5% for <em>NTRK1</em> and <em>NTRK3 </em>in most series from non&ndash;radiation-associated papillary carcinoma in adult patients; the prevalence is higher in children and young patients and in radiation-associated papillary carcinoma. <sup>f</sup><em>EIF1AX </em>mutations occur in <em>RAS</em>-mutated tumours. <sup>g</sup>The mutation burden per tumour is estimated from TCGA Research Network, 2014 </span><span class=\"Ref-PMID\" style=\"color: #984806; background: #ccc0d9;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\">{25417114}</span></span><span lang=\"EN-GB\">; Landa et al., 2016 </span><span class=\"Ref-PMID\" style=\"color: #984806; background: #ccc0d9;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\">{26878173}</span></span><span lang=\"EN-GB\">; and Pozdeyev et al., 2018 </span><span class=\"Ref-PMID\" style=\"color: #984806; background: #ccc0d9;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\">{29615459}</span></span><span lang=\"EN-GB\">. <sup>h</sup>TCGA Research Network, 2014 </span><span class=\"Ref-PMID\" style=\"color: #984806; background: #ccc0d9;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\">{25417114}</span></span><span lang=\"EN-GB\">.</span></p>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\">Note: The main molecular alterations are shown, with the estimated ranges of mutation prevalence.</span></p>",
